// =============================================================================
// AI-103 Lesson 11 -- Query C: error taxonomy
//
// "What is actually going wrong, and how often?" Error analysis is a frozen
// objective for this lesson, and the useful version groups failures by KIND
// rather than listing them one by one.
//
// The demos deliberately generate an unhappy path (an invoice ID that does not
// exist), because "the tool found nothing" is the most common real failure an
// agent hits in production -- and it is NOT an exception, so it never shows up
// in a naive success == false filter. Both shapes are covered below.
//
// Paste into: Application Insights -> Logs
// =============================================================================
// Part 1 -- hard failures: spans that actually errored.
dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(24h)
| where success == false
| extend
    component = tostring(split(name, " ")[0]),
    subject   = tostring(split(name, " ")[1])
| summarize
    occurrences = count(),
    example     = any(name),
    last_seen   = max(timestamp)
    by component, subject, resultCode
| order by occurrences desc
